/-
Johnson/Road/K4/K04LawR.lean: THE KIND K4's SHARE OF THE CHAIN OF PROMISES IN THE SECOND FORM: IT
ENDS IN THE COUNT's FORM, AT THE COMPOSED MEANING `mgAll 𝔇 mgBase` OVER A LETTER 𝔇, AT A LETTER FOR
THE EXTRACTOR AND A LETTER FOR THE ROW OF PIECES. A LEMMA OF THE ASSEMBLY: K04LawAt.lean and
K04LawKind.lean call it; the end by the count's own name stands in the latter.
No new argument. IT PAYS NOTHING.

FIRST. NO MEMBER OF ITS BINDERS IS SHOWN ANYWHERE. K04_law IS NOT PROVED BY THIS. OF ITS DECIDABLE
BINDERS: NONE IS KNOWN TO BE FALSE AT THE WIDER MEANING: `K4RowPlan`'s TESTS THAT READ THE MEANING's
DOOR ARE DECIDED BY THE KERNEL AT THE WIDER MEANING's OWN CLOSED DOOR, WITH NEGATIVE TESTS (fields
here: not called); sealLast AND blocksOk HAVE BEEN EVALUATED TRUE AT BOTH
SIZES, WITH NEGATIVE TESTS (a run, not shown here). (LOOKED AT, BY READING, NOT COMPILED: the
wider meaning's "in order" has sign for sign the form that `K4Means.inOrder` asks, at Dk.base := the
base's own and the composed meaning's letters: the equation that is false at the composed meaning
itself can hold here.) OF THE WIDER MEANING: it is no reference form: the
composed meaning stays the one constant that counts: the wider meaning is one side of a bridge: a
law shown at it counts only when the bridge is paid.

  `k04_law_R`: in the goals' scope, at an opening of the IOP as written in Lean, at pieces that are
    the maker's cut: `KindTiedR Dk.N (mgAll 𝔇 mgBase) linksFull (flatPlacesOf linksFull true)
    (RchPub (descAt Z A B c) Pp) E (T.p₁ :: T.l₁) KindName.K4`, AT EVERY CONDITION Pp ON THE PUBLIC
    PART. THE MEANING IS THE TERM mgAll 𝔇 mgBase OVER A LETTER 𝔇 (with the struck parts' data Ew, a
    letter, and its own base `mgBase`): FOUR OF 𝔇's FIELDS HAVE THE VERY TYPE OF A SENTENCE OF A
    MEANING (cr1, wt, headPart, digitsPart); K4 reads three of them: SO THIS IS NOT "AT THE
    CONSTANT". The condition beside the promise is a term over the letter
    Pp: `RchPub`: some views lead the IOP's own run from the first state to this state (`RchAt`),
    and Pp holds of the public part; THE SAME CONDITION STANDS IN Sp.

ITS BINDERS, IN THREE LOTS. (1) ALL OF `k04_law_of`'s (K04LawOf.lean), TO THE TOKEN (held by
program), AT THE WIDER MEANING `mgWide 𝔇 Ew mgBase` IN THE PLACE OF ITS LETTER Mg, BUT ONE: the
scope (hS, hR), the opening (O), the pieces (hT, hD, hs, hc, hcap), hok, the data Dk with hnR and
hkC, `K4Means` (Em) AT THE WIDER MEANING, hE, lw, and the families `K4RowAt`, `K4LaterAt`,
`K4FirstAt`; OF `K4NameAt`'s THREE FIELDS TWO STAY (hWi, hNf); THE THIRD, THE TEST openNext, IS NO
BINDER: it is `Rec.openNext_mgWide`, out of a decision by the kernel at
the wider meaning's own closed door, with two negative tests (at the composed meaning's own door it
rejects at each of the twelve). (2) THE BRIDGE's: THE TIGHT LIST (
"no fold fact in front of it is unpaid" means what the row SPENDS:
IT IS WHAT THE BRIDGE SPENDS: at least seven of the nineteen clauses are read by no line of
K4's own argument but the keeping): Sp: AT K4's OWN TWENTY-FOUR BORDERS 28 g + 4 AND 28 g + 5 ALONE,
at every state that the IOP's run reaches there without a mark and whose public part meets Pp:
`K4Spends`: THE FIFTEEN FACTS THAT THE BRIDGE SPENDS (`WideFacts`, MgWideFacts.lean, each under the
name of its field in `FoldFacts`, at 𝔇's and Ew's own numbers: bookInOrder, seatsCarried, bookFits,
msgShapes, weightsOk, pileMasks, pileWithin, oneRow, tidy, codes, shape, layout, liveShape,
liveLayout, reqIs), and the tests of "pile.room", "K8.lay7", "K8.onThird", "K8.funsThird" where
these names are open there at the wider door. By the pointwise `factsAt_at` (
Johnson/Desc/Sound/MgWideFacts.lean). `k04_law_R_fold`: THE COROLLARY: the form with
the one structure: `FoldFacts`, `FoldTies`, `RoomOpen`, `K8Open` at every border give Sp: for the
join at the top. (3) NOTHING MORE: of the bridge's other premises, the test on the two doors is
`Rec.doorsFit_mgWide`, out of a decision by the kernel at K4's twenty-four
borders with two negative tests; "at the base every name of the class has its sentence" is
`classA_said`, out of the written table First.saysNone (AllSaid.lean); "outside the class the wider
tests are the composed meaning's" and "the wider in-order gives the composed one's" are lemmas of
Johnson/Desc/Sound/MgWide.lean (called in K04LawAtWide.lean); "an accepting run of the piece hands
the condition on" is `handsOn_pub` (Johnson/Top/H0/Walk/ReachPub.lean), from hT: called here.

WHAT IS NO BINDER AND IS OWED ALL THE SAME. THE
FRONT: the counted form begins at the laid IOP and the plan's test, where this has nine binders on
the pieces. Dk IS A LETTER HERE (a term in K04LawAt.lean). Dk's d12, free0 AND fvs ARE TIED BY
`K4Means`' EQUATIONS AND, THROUGH Sp's room, TO THE LEDGER OF EVERY REACHED UNMARKED STATE AT WHICH
THE NAME IS OPEN (of the form at every border: "fvs := []" is then no way out
wherever one state is reached behind the first clearing; UNDER THE TIGHT LIST THAT HOLDS ONLY AS FAR
AS THE NAME IS OPEN AT K4's OWN BORDERS: K4's place asks it, by the kernel's row on the door; that
it is open at both borders is not shown here). Dk.base IS A LETTER OF Dk:
`K4Means.inOrder` ties it to the base's own "in order", which is true everywhere at `mgBase`. THAT
DOES NOT SHUT EVERY IDLE CHOICE: 𝔇 IS A LETTER: at a 𝔇 whose reader of
the request never reads back, the composed meaning's "in order" is false everywhere, no unmarked
state lies inside the promise, and the end is worth nothing: no emptiness of the binders; an idle
end. "onlineDescription returns", inside the opening, has an evaluated example and no proved one.

Limits. EVERY BINDER IS A PREMISE. SHOWN TOGETHER AT NO DATA. The second hash function and the
reference sizes alone. Nothing on soundness.
-/
